  "notes": "{掲示|けいじ} refers to the public posting or display of information such as announcements, schedules, and results. Also functions as a する verb.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]を{掲示|けいじ}する\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {掲示|けいじ}する: to post, to display publicly\n- {掲示|けいじ}{板|ばん}: bulletin board\n- {掲示|けいじ}{物|ぶつ}: posted notice/material\n- {掲示|けいじ}を{見|み}る: to check the notice board\n\nDIGITAL:\n- {電子|でんし}{掲示|けいじ}{板|ばん}: electronic bulletin board, BBS (often abbreviated to {掲示|けいじ}{板|ばん} online)\n- ネット{掲示|けいじ}{板|ばん}: internet forum\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n{刑事|けいじ} (detective/criminal case) has the same reading but completely different meaning and kanji.\n\nUSAGE:\nCommonly encountered at schools, universities, train stations, and government offices where public notices are posted.",
